items.content:
@flawedaxioms This seems to be a BS claim; I can't find *any* data to back it up and I searched quite a bit. If it were true, SaaS stocks would have be skyrocketing; in fact they have been crashing.

SWE employment at SaaS companies has been flat, and revenue has been 100% tracking long-term trends that predate AI.

ADBE, WDAY, ZM, CRM are good examples of SaaS revenue trends. Completely steady over time; zero disruption or acceleration from AI.

Building safer AI agents takes more than model safeguards.

@perplexity_ai open sourced SPACE, the agent sandbox platform behind Computer, giving developers more control over where agents run code and what they can access.

Cheers to more teams open-sourcing tools to build safer autonomous AI agents.

